I will implement a "Connection Probe" mechanism in `App.tsx`.

**The Problem:** Currently, the application attempts to initialize three Firestore listeners (Users, Missions, Settings) simultaneously at startup. If the API is not enabled, all three fail and log separate red errors to the console, creating a noisy and alarming debugging experience.

**The Solution:**
1.  I will verify the connection with a single, lightweight `getDoc` request first.
2.  If this probe fails (Permission Denied), I immediately switch to Offline Mode and **block** the other listeners from ever starting.
3.  This reduces the number of console errors from ~3-4 down to just 1 (the probe failure), which is much cleaner.

